# ============================================================================
# FlowConjugateHeat / closed box: a cold plate and a warm gas come to equilibrium  (Hydro2, ablation.conduction = 1)
#
# Periodic slabs (solid fraction 0.32 of the period 0.4472; rho_s cp_s = 3.5, k_s = k_g, T_s0 = 0.9) between layers of
# gas at rest (rho 1, p 1, T 1; cv 2.5; k_g 4.861e-3).  Nothing crosses the boundary (periodic), so
#   * the total energy  int_gas rho E dx + rho_s cp_s int_solid T_s dx  is constant,
#   * the gas mass is constant, and
#   * both end at  T_eq = (m_g cv T_g0 + C_s T_s0)/(m_g cv + C_s) = 0.96004   (gas at constant volume),
#     with p_eq = p0 T_eq/T_g0.
# Checks that the fluid|solid thermal coupling neither creates nor loses energy over a long time and that the two
# sides settle at the same temperature.  The solid receives the stage-weighted surface flux the gas conduction used
# (energy-conservative exchange, 2026-10-06).  Measured: T_eq 0.960039 (exact 0.960039), energy change -1.9e-7 of the
# total, the same at cfl 0.3 and 0.15.  (Before that change the balance closed only to first order in dt: 0.21 /
# 0.10 / 0.05 % of the heat exchanged at cfl 0.3 / 0.15 / 0.075.)
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 2 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowConjugateHeat/input_1D_ClosedBoxEquilibrium plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowConjugateHeat/reference/closed_box_check.py <dir> [<dir with a smaller time step> ...]
